{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStoreGuide","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Keys","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KVKey"],"title":"Keys"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore"],"anchor":"Protocol","title":"Protocol"},{"anchor":"Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UserDefaultsKeyValueStore","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeychainKeyValueStore","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/InMemoryKeyValueStore"],"title":"Implementations"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Persist scalar preferences like theme, sort order, or last-seen version — testably, with type-safe keys."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/keyvaluestoreguide"]}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginKillswitchReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginParentalGateReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginAnalyticsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted"],"anchor":"Reference","title":"Reference"}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"role":"collectionGroup","title":"KeyValueStore","roleHeading":"API Collection"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore"},{"type":"text","text":" is a small protocol for one-shot scalar values that don’t fit"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"type":"text","text":" model. Three implementations ship:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UserDefaultsKeyValueStore","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" — production, backed by any "},{"code":"UserDefaults","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" suite"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeychainKeyValueStore","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" — production, backed by the system Keychain (survives reinstall)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/InMemoryKeyValueStore","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" — tests, dictionary-backed, reference semantics"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Inject through your "},{"code":"Environment","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", hydrate state at startup, and write from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"effects. Reducers stay pure."}]},{"code":["public protocol KeyValueStore: Sendable {","    func value<Value>(_ key: KVKey<Value>) -> Value?","    func setValue<Value>(_ value: Value?, for key: KVKey<Value>)","    func removeValue<Value>(for key: KVKey<Value>)","    func contains<Value>(_ key: KVKey<Value>) -> Bool","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"All values are JSON-encoded as ","type":"text"},{"code":"Data","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Reads and writes go through ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KVKey","type":"reference"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which pairs a backing-store name with its ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value type at compile time.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"When to Use What","level":2,"anchor":"When-to-Use-What","type":"heading"},{"rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Need"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use"}]}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Collection of identifiable entities (decks, cards, sessions)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" + "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"reference"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Scalar preference (theme, sort order, last-seen version)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore"},{"type":"text","text":" (UserDefaults)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Anonymous device identity that must survive reinstall"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore"},{"type":"text","text":" (Keychain)"}]}]]],"header":"row","type":"table"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"EntityStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is for many-of-a-kind data with change tracking and batched"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"writes. "},{"code":"KeyValueStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is for one-of-a-kind values that you read once at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"startup and overwrite on change."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"UserDefaults vs Keychain","level":3,"anchor":"UserDefaults-vs-Keychain","type":"heading"},{"rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UserDefaultsKeyValueStore"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeychainKeyValueStore"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Survives reinstall?"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes (this-device-only by default)"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Backup \/ device migration"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Included"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Excluded with default accessibility"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Throughput"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Fast (in-memory cache)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Slower (system call)"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Visible to other apps?"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No (per app\/group)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Optionally (App Groups via "},{"code":"accessGroup:","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Best for"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Theme, sort order, feature toggles, last-seen version"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Anonymous device ID, opaque tokens"}]}]]],"header":"row","type":"table"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Keychain costs more per access — hydrate once at launch and observe state"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"afterward, never read inside a reducer."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"macOS sandbox & entitlements","level":3,"anchor":"macOS-sandbox--entitlements","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"KeychainKeyValueStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" uses the data-protection keychain, so it never raises"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a user prompt — no “Always Allow \/ Deny” dialog, no locked-keychain prompt, no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Touch ID \/ Face ID challenge."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"tip","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"sandboxed"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" macOS app still needs a keychain entitlement, even when"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not sharing items across an access group. Xcode supplies an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"application-identifier","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" automatically for provisioning-profile–signed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"builds; otherwise add an explicit "},{"code":"keychain-access-groups","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" entry:"}]},{"code":["<key>keychain-access-groups<\/key>","<array>","    <string>$(AppIdentifierPrefix)com.example.myapp<\/string>","<\/array>"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"xml"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Without it, the first "},{"code":"setValue","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" fails with "},{"code":"errSecMissingEntitlement","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"code":"OSStatus","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" −34018). This is a build\/signing condition, not a runtime"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"prompt. iOS \/ iPadOS \/ tvOS \/ watchOS need no extra entitlement."}]}],"name":"Tip","type":"aside"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Encryption, accessibility, iCloud-sync exclusion, and backup exclusion are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"identical whichever entitlement you use — the access group only controls"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"which of your own apps"}]},{"type":"text","text":" can read an item, never third parties or the cloud."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"For a private device ID, in order of strictness:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Most private:"}]},{"type":"text","text":" profile-signed build + "},{"code":"accessGroup: nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", relying on the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"implicit "},{"code":"application-identifier","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" group. No other app — even same-team —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can be entitled to it. Mirrors the iOS default; zero sharing surface."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Practically equivalent:"}]},{"type":"text","text":" a "},{"code":"keychain-access-groups","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" array whose only"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"entry is the team-prefixed bundle id (the snippet above). Use when a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"profile-signed build isn’t available (unsigned local \/ CI dev). Only delta:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a same-team app you sign could also declare that string."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Intentional sharing only:"}]},{"type":"text","text":" a shared group string. The "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"first"}]},{"type":"text","text":" element"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"becomes the default group for new items — never put a shared group first"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for private data."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"orderedList"},{"text":"Device-Identity Pattern","level":2,"anchor":"Device-Identity-Pattern","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The original motivation for "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeychainKeyValueStore"},{"type":"text","text":" was apps without user"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"auth that still want stable identity for analytics. Mint a UUID once with the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore\/deviceIdentity(key:)"},{"type":"text","text":" helper, hydrate into "},{"code":"AppState","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" at launch,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and feed it to "},{"code":"AnalyticsIdentity","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". The "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"same"}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"deviceID","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is also the stable"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"feature-flag bucketing identity (the plugin’s "},{"code":"deviceIDKeyPath","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), so analytics"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and A\/B exposure share one identity:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["\/\/ `KVKey.deviceID` and `deviceIdentity()` ship with Swidux.","","\/\/ In Store.configured(), before constructing the store:","let kv = KeychainKeyValueStore(service: \"com.example.myapp\")","let deviceID = kv.deviceIdentity()   \/\/ reads, or mints-and-persists, a stable UUID","","let initialState = AppState(deviceID: deviceID, \/* … *\/)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Then in the analytics plugin wiring:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["AnalyticsPlugin(","    service: analytics,","    identity: AnalyticsIdentity(userID: \\.deviceID, properties: { _ in [:] }),","    \/\/ …",")"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The closure-based "},{"code":"userID","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" keypath runs on every dispatch, so the value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"must"}]},{"type":"text","text":" live in state — never call into the Keychain from the closure. Hydrate"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"once; observe state."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Type-safe Keys","level":2,"anchor":"Type-safe-Keys","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Declare each key once on "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KVKey"},{"type":"text","text":" so the value type travels with the name —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"no magic strings at call sites:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["extension KVKey where Value == Theme {","    static let theme = KVKey<Theme>(\"theme\")","}","","extension KVKey where Value == SortOrder {","    static let sortOrder = KVKey<SortOrder>(\"sortOrder\")","}","","extension KVKey where Value == String {","    static let lastSeenVersion = KVKey<String>(\"lastSeenVersion\")","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Then read and write through static-member literals. The compiler enforces"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that the value type matches what you declared:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let theme = store.value(.theme) ?? .system            \/\/ Theme?","store.setValue(theme, for: .theme)","store.setValue(.alphabetical, for: .sortOrder)","store.removeValue(for: .lastSeenVersion)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A typo or wrong type produces a compile error, not a silent miss at runtime."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Centralizing keys on "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KVKey"},{"type":"text","text":" also gives you autocomplete and a single place"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to audit your preference surface."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Wiring","level":2,"anchor":"Wiring","type":"heading"},{"text":"1. Add to your environment","level":3,"anchor":"1-Add-to-your-environment","type":"heading"},{"code":["struct AppEnvironment: Sendable {","    var keyValue: any KeyValueStore","","    static func live() -> AppEnvironment {","        AppEnvironment(keyValue: UserDefaultsKeyValueStore())","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"text":"2. Hydrate at startup","level":3,"anchor":"2-Hydrate-at-startup","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Read once into the initial state — never read mid-cycle from a reducer."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["extension AppState {","    static func hydrated(from store: any KeyValueStore) -> AppState {","        AppState(","            theme: store.value(.theme) ?? .system,","            sortOrder: store.value(.sortOrder) ?? .alphabetical,","            lastSeenVersion: store.value(.lastSeenVersion)","        )","    }","}","","let env = AppEnvironment.live()","let store = AppStore.configured(state: .hydrated(from: env.keyValue), environment: env)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"text":"3. Write from an effect","level":3,"anchor":"3-Write-from-an-effect","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Mutate state in the reducer, return an effect that writes the value:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["case .themeChanged(let theme):","    state.theme = theme","    return { @Sendable _ in","        environment.keyValue.setValue(theme, for: .theme)","    }"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No "},{"code":"try?","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", no "},{"code":"do\/catch","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore\/setValue(_:for:)"},{"type":"text","text":" does not throw —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"encoder errors are programmer mistakes (e.g. "},{"code":"Float.nan","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), so the store logs"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them and triggers "},{"code":"assertionFailure","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in DEBUG instead of forcing every effect"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to handle an "},{"code":"Error","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" it can’t act on."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Testing","level":2,"anchor":"Testing","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Inject "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/InMemoryKeyValueStore"},{"type":"text","text":" and assert against the same instance:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["@Test","@MainActor","func themeChangePersists() async throws {","    let prefs = InMemoryKeyValueStore()","    let env = AppEnvironment(keyValue: prefs)","    let store = AppStore.configured(state: AppState(), environment: env)","","    try await confirmation(expectedCount: 1) { confirm in","        store.send(.themeChanged(.dark))","","        for _ in 0..<50 {","            if prefs.value(.theme) == .dark {","                confirm()","                break","            }","            try await Task.sleep(for: .milliseconds(10))","        }","    }","","    \/\/ Simulate a relaunch.","    let rehydrated = AppState.hydrated(from: prefs)","    #expect(rehydrated.theme == .dark)","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Tests touching real "},{"code":"UserDefaults","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" should use a fresh per-test suite and tear"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it down explicitly:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let suiteName = \"myapp.tests.\\(UUID().uuidString)\"","let defaults = UserDefaults(suiteName: suiteName)!","defer { defaults.removePersistentDomain(forName: suiteName) }","","let store = UserDefaultsKeyValueStore(suite: defaults)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"text":"Reads Are For Hydration","level":2,"anchor":"Reads-Are-For-Hydration","type":"heading"},{"style":"important","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reading from "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore"},{"type":"text","text":" mid-cycle (inside a reducer) is an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"anti-pattern. Reducers must be pure and synchronous; reads happen once at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"AppState","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" construction. After hydration, the value lives in state and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"downstream code observes state, not the store."}]}],"name":"Important","type":"aside"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"UserDefaults","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" itself is thread-safe, but a reducer reading while an effect"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"writes creates ordering ambiguity. Hydrate, observe state, write through"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"effects — that’s the discipline."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Failure Modes","level":2,"anchor":"Failure-Modes","type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Missing key"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore\/value(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" returns "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Provide a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"default at the call site."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Decode failure"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — returns "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and logs through "},{"code":"os.Logger","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(subsystem "},{"code":"\"swidux\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", category "},{"code":"\"kvstore\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"). On startup, behaves identically"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to first launch."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Encode failure"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — logged at the same subsystem\/category, then"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"assertionFailure","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" fires in DEBUG so the bug surfaces during development."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Production builds log and continue; the in-memory state is unchanged. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"API does not throw — there is no useful runtime recovery from inside an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"effect, and "},{"code":"try?","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" would just hide the problem."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"text":"@AppStorage Interop","level":2,"anchor":"AppStorage-Interop","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"There is none, by design. "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UserDefaultsKeyValueStore"},{"type":"text","text":" writes JSON-encoded"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"Data","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" blobs. SwiftUI’s "},{"code":"@AppStorage","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" only observes native primitive types"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"code":"Bool","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"String","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"URL","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", raw "},{"code":"Data","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"). Two parallel"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"observation channels — Swidux state and "},{"code":"@AppStorage","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — would drift."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux state is the source of truth. Read once at hydration, then observe"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"state through the store."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Schema Migration","level":2,"anchor":"Schema-Migration","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Out of scope for "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore"},{"type":"text","text":". If a "},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" shape changes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"incompatibly, declare a new versioned key:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["\/\/ before:","extension KVKey where Value == Theme {","    static let theme = KVKey<Theme>(\"theme\")","}","\/\/ after a breaking shape change:","extension KVKey where Value == Theme {","    static let theme = KVKey<Theme>(\"theme.v2\")","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Old keys can be cleaned up at startup with "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore\/removeValue(for:)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(declare a tombstone "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KVKey"},{"type":"text","text":" of any value type — only the name is read)."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoRedo":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","type":"topic","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Add stack-based undo\/redo to your app with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoredo","title":"Undo \/ Redo"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/KVKey":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KVKey","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"KVKey","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A type-safe key for "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"KVKey","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/kvkey","title":"KVKey"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/KeyValueStore/value(_:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStore\/value(_:)","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns the decoded value, or "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" if the key is absent or its payload"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fails to decode as "},{"code":"Value","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Decode failures are logged."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"ke